t)}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}-2s},\\,s>2.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${f}^{′}$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043469/state.json" "file_sha256" "e52351906530253ebc5b56d0f7f6ea7051165295ec0f612ec4affb499e653caa"} {"question" "q-79442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ where $f(t)$ is a continuous function of exponential order $a$ on $[0,\\infty ).$ If ${f}^{′}(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ),$ then\n\n$$\nL{{f}^{′}(t)}=sL{f(t)}-f(0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the Laplace transform of ${f}^{′}(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{′}(t)} & =sL{f(t)}-f(0) \\\\  & =s\\cdot \\frac{2}{{s}^{2}-2s}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{2s}{s(s-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043469/state.json" "file_sha256" "e52351906530253ebc5b56d0f7f6ea7051165295ec0f612ec4affb499e653caa"} {"question" "q-79442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043469/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2549b21413bed12d2711c3005d2a0accf2b05a23ad17e834574c47dea483c33a"} {"question" "q-79442" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043469/state.json" "file_sha256" "e52351906530253ebc5b56d0f7f6ea7051165295ec0f612ec4affb499e653caa"} {"question" "q-79442" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2s-1}{s-2}"] ["math" "\\frac{2s}{s-2}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{s-2}"] ["math" "\\frac{s+1}{s-