\frac{10s-12}{{s}^{2}-4s+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043469/state.json" "file_sha256" "e52351906530253ebc5b56d0f7f6ea7051165295ec0f612ec4affb499e653caa"} {"question" "q-79443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043469/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2549b21413bed12d2711c3005d2a0accf2b05a23ad17e834574c47dea483c33a"} {"question" "q-79443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043469/state.json" "file_sha256" "e52351906530253ebc5b56d0f7f6ea7051165295ec0f612ec4affb499e653caa"} {"question" "q-79443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{10s-12}{{s}^{2}-4s+3}"] ["math" "\\frac{12s-9}{{s}^{2}-4s+3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3s-4}{{s}^{2}-4s+3}"] ["math" "\\frac{4s-3}{{s}^{2}-4s+3}"] ["math" "\\frac{8s-6}{{s}^{2}-4s+3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043469/state.json" "file_sha256" "e52351906530253ebc5b56d0f7f6ea7051165295ec0f612ec4affb499e653caa"} {"question" "q-79443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{10s-12}{{s}^{2}-4s+3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043469/state.json" "file_sha256" "e52351906530253ebc5b56d0f7f6ea7051165295ec0f612ec4affb499e653caa"} {"question" "q-64408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Laplace transform $L{{f}^{″}(t)}$ for $s>1,$ given that the function $f(t)$ is continuous on $[0,\\infty ),$ ${f}^{′}(0)=-1,$ $f(0)=2,$ and\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=\\frac{2s+1}{{s}^{2}+s-2},\\,s>1.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${f}^{′}$ is continuous and ${f}^{″}$ piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043469/state.json" "file_sha256" "e52351906530253ebc5b56d0f7f6ea7051165295ec0f612ec4affb499e653caa"} {"question" "q-64408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ where $f(t)$ is a continuous function of exponential order $a$ on $[0,\\infty ).$ If ${f}^{′}(t)$ is continuous and ${f}^{″}(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ),$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{″}(t)} & ={s}^{2}L{f(t)}-sf(0)-{f}^{′}(0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the Laplace transform of ${f}^{″}(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{″}(t)} & ={s}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2s+1}{{s}^{2}+s-2}-s\\cdot 2-(-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{s}^{2}(2s+1)}{{s}^{2}+s-2}-(2s-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{s}^{2}(2s+1)-({s}^{2}+s-2)(2s-1)}{{s}^{2}+s-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{s}^{2}(2s+1)-{s}^{2}(2s-1)-(s-2)(2s-1)}{{s}^{2}+s-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-(2{s}^{2}-5s+2)}{{s}^{2}+s-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5s-2}{{s}^{2}+s-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043469/state.json" "file_sha256" "e52351906530253ebc5b56d0f7f6ea7051165295ec0f612ec4affb499e653caa"} {"question" "q-64408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043469/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2549b21413bed12d2711c3005d2a0accf2b05a23ad17e834574c47dea483c33a"} {"question" "q-64408" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "