 $s > 0,$ given that the function $f(t)$ is continuous on $[0,\\infty),$ $f'(0)=2,$ $f(0)=-1,$ and\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{f(t)\\right\\} =   \\dfrac{2 - s}{s^2+4}, \\quad s>0.\n$$\n\nAssume that $f'$ is continuous and $f''$ piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043469/example-6649.json" "file_sha256" "71eb6090ed9d060b109f74ecff85d26a1944b6c10a543c8bf59ccf34bab5a00e"} {"question" "e-6649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $F(s) = \\mathcal L \\{f(t)\\}$ where $f(t)$ is a continuous function of exponential order $a$ on $[0,\\infty).$ If $f'(t)$ is continuous and $f''(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty),$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{″}(t)} & ={s}^{2}L{f(t)}-sf(0)-{f}^{′}(0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the Laplace transform of $f''(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{″}(t)} & ={s}^{2}L{f(t)}-sf(0)-{f}^{′}(0) \\\\  & ={s}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2-s}{{s}^{2}+4}-s\\cdot (-1)-2 \\\\  & =\\frac{{s}^{2}(2-s)}{{s}^{2}+4}+s-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{{s}^{2}(s-2)}{{s}^{2}+4}+(s-2) \\\\  & =(s-2)(-\\frac{{s}^{2}}{{s}^{2}+4}+1) \\\\  & =(s-2)(\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4(s-2)}{{s}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s > 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043469/example-6649.json" "file_sha256" "71eb6090ed9d060b109f74ecff85d26a1944b6c10a543c8bf59ccf34bab5a00e"}] "usage" {"e-6648" [] "q-64323" [] "e-6649" []} "basis" 1617 "retractions" [[17592186148091 :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform of $f^{′}(t)$ for $s > 3$ given that the function $f(t)$ is continuous over $[MATH: [0, ∞),]$ $f(0) = 2$, and\n\n$L{f(t)} = \\frac{2s - 1}{s^{2} - s - 6}, s > 3$.\nAssume that $f^{′}$ is piecewise continuous on $[MATH: [0, ∞).]$"] [17592186147297 :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform of $f'(t)$ for $s > 3$ given that the function $f(t)$ is continuous over $[MATH: [0,\\infty),]$ $f(0)=0$, and\n$\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{f(t)\\right\\} = \\dfrac{6}{s^2-5s+6}, \\quad s>3$.\nAssume that $f'$ is piecewise continuous on $[MATH: [0,\\infty).]$"] [17592186147297 :question/worked-solution "Suppose\n\n$$\nF(s) = \\mathcal L \\{f(t)\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(t)$ is a continuous function of exponential order $a$ on $[MATH: [0,\\infty).]$ If $f'(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[MATH: [0,\\infty),]$ then\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{f'(t) \\right\\} = s \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{f(t) \\right\\} - f(0)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the Laplace transform of $f'(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{f^{′}(t)} &= sL{f(t)} - f(0) \\\\\n&= s \\cdot \\frac{6}{s^{2} - 5s + 6} - 0 \\\\\n&= \\frac{6s}{s^{2} - 5s + 6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s > 3$."] [17592186147298 :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{f''(t) \\right\\}$ for $s > 0$, given that the function $f(t)$ is continuous on $[MATH: [0,\\infty),]$ $f'(0)=2$, $f(0)=-1$, and\n$\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{f(t)\\right\\} = \\dfrac{2 - s}{s^2+4}, \\quad s>0$.\nAssume that $f'$ is continuous and $f''$ piecewise continuous on $[MATH: [0,\\infty).]$"] [17592186147298 :question/worked-solution "Suppose\n\n$$\nF(s) = \\mathcal L \\{f(t)\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(t)$ is a continuous function of exponential order $a$ on $[MATH: [0,\\infty).]$ If $f'(t)$ is continuous and $f''(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[MATH: [0,\\infty),]$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{f^{″}(t)} &= s^{2}L{f(t)} - sf(0) - f^{′}(0)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the Laplace transform of $f''(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{f^{″}(t)} &= s^{2}L{f(t)} - sf(0) - f^{′}(0) \\\\\n&= s^{2} \\cdot \\frac{2 - s}{s^{2} + 4} - s \\cdot (-1) - 2 \\\\\n&= (s^{2}(2 - s))/(s^{2} + 4) + s - 2 \\\\\n&= - (s^{2}(s - 2))/(s^{2} + 4) + (s - 2) \\\\\n&= (s - 2)(-\\frac{s^{2}}{s^{2} + 4} + 1) \\\\\n&= (s - 2)(\\frac{4}{s^{2} + 4}) \\\\\n&= (4(s - 2))/(s^{2} + 4)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s > 0$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186146558 17592186146559 17592186146560 17592186146561 17592186146562] "immutable_fields" [[17592186146557 :answer-field/correct] [17592186146557 :answer-field/id] [17592186146557 :answer-field/key] [17592186146557 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
